{
  "name": "Urban Studies and Planning - BA",
  "kind": "major",
  "type": "Bachelor's Degree",
  "department": "Urban Studies and Planning",
  "source": "https://catalog.ucsd.edu/curric/USP.html",
  "narrative": [
    "The undergraduate program in urban studies and planning requires six lower-division courses in urban studies and planning, and twelve courses in upper-division urban studies and planning.",
    "All lower-division and upper-division requirements must be taken for a letter grade. A 2.0 grade point average is required in the major, and students must earn at least C– in each course used for the major.",
    "No more than one special studies course, USP 198 or USP 199, will be accepted to count toward the major.",
    "Courses used to satisfy the major cannot be applied toward a minor, although some overlap is allowed for double majors.",
    "Because the senior sequence includes an internship, no other internship or field placement will be counted toward the major.",
    "Students are required to complete USP 30, USP 60, USP 124, a research methods course, and a technical elective course prior to enrolling in USP 186. USP 186 is a prerequisite for USP 187.",
    "USP courses numbered 150–159 are reserved for the real estate and development major and do not count toward USP major requirements."
  ],
